//! Host-embedding surface for the web API bindings.
//!
//! This module defines the pieces of the bindings that the rest of the
//! crate needs whether or not the web APIs are installed:
//!
//! * [`JsInvoker`] — invokes JS function values from host code (event
//!   listeners, timer bodies, microtasks, promise reactions). Implemented
//!   by [`Vm`](crate::vm::Vm).
//! * [`ScriptEngine`] — evaluates script source; implemented by
//!   [`Vm`](crate::vm::Vm). [`ScriptError`] reports its failures.
//! * [`ContextId`] / [`web_apis`] — the thread-local registry of live
//!   [`WebApis`] states, keyed by context id.
//! * [`ApiError`] — installation failures.
//! * [`WebApis`] — the per-context state: document tree, listeners,
//!   promises, timers, fetch machinery, wrapper caches.
//!
//! # Installation
//!
//! Two entry points plant the web APIs on a page global:
//!
//! * [`install_web_apis`] — the full surface: `window`, `document`,
//!   `location`, `navigator`, `fetch`, `setTimeout`/`clearTimeout`/
//!   `queueMicrotask`, `setInterval`/`requestAnimationFrame` (via
//!   [`install_timers`](crate::bindings_timers::install_timers)),
//!   `getComputedStyle`, plus the storage/history extensions
//!   ([`install_storage`](crate::bindings_storage::install_storage))
//!   and `URL`/`URLSearchParams`/encoding
//!   ([`install_url`](crate::bindings_url::install_url)). Takes the heap,
//!   global, document, event loop, and invoker explicitly; the unit tests
//!   drive it with fakes.
//! * [`Vm::install_page_web_apis`] — the production path, called once
//!   per page realm by `bowser_app::script::PageVm` (an inherent method
//!   on the exported [`Vm`], so it needs no new crate-root exports).
//!   Installs everything the full entry point does, timer/microtask
//!   globals included (`setTimeout`, `clearTimeout`, `setInterval`,
//!   `clearInterval`, `queueMicrotask`, `requestAnimationFrame`,
//!   `cancelAnimationFrame`): those shadow the VM's own timer
//!   intrinsics, and firing the bindings' timer callbacks from the
//!   event-loop pump goes through the pump hook
//!   ([`pump_page_event_loop`]), which evals the hidden
//!   [`FIRE_TASK_KEY`] native so the [`ReentrantInvoker`] can re-enter
//!   the interpreter (see its contract). Page `setTimeout` and friends
//!   therefore fire through the realm's `pump`
//!   (`bowser_app::script::PageVm::pump`).
//!   [`Vm::remove_page_web_apis`] tears the installation down.
//!
//! # The invoker
//!
//! [`install_web_apis`] takes an explicit `invoker:
//! Rc<RefCell<dyn JsInvoker>>`; the production path uses
//! [`ReentrantInvoker`], which re-enters the currently-executing VM
//! through the engine's sanctioned native-to-JS choke point. It works
//! wherever a native is on the stack (event-listener dispatch from
//! `dispatchEvent`, and the page pump's hidden [`FIRE_TASK_KEY`] native)
//! and fails closed elsewhere.
//!
//! # Embedder notes
//!
//! * **Reentrancy discipline.** A [`WebApis`] borrow is never held across
//!   a [`JsInvoker::call`] or [`ScriptEngine::evaluate`]. Native functions
//!   and the runner borrow briefly, extract what they need, drop the guard,
//!   then invoke JS. Violating this panics on the `RefCell`.
//! * **`window === globalThis`.** Everything is installed directly on the
//!   global object and `window` is a self-reference. A real browser keeps
//!   `Window` distinct from the global scope chain; v1 does not.
//! * **Interior mutability.** Native functions only receive `&mut Heap`,
//!   so the `Document` is shared as `Rc<RefCell<Document>>` rather than
//!   `&mut Document`. The embedder keeps a clone; both see the same tree.
//! * **`:visited` privacy.** `getComputedStyle` must never reveal
//!   visited-link state (it would leak browsing history). Style
//!   computation goes through `bowser_css::compute_style`, which matches
//!   selectors with `matches` — i.e. `matches_with_state` under
//!   `ElementState::default()` with `visited: false` — so the styling
//!   pipeline is never given the real visited bit.
//! * **Teardown.** Call [`remove_context`] when the page goes away (tab
//!   close / navigation); it cancels in-flight fetches and drops the
//!   timer/storage state. Wrapper objects already handed to JS keep
//!   working until their heap dies, but host calls then fail with "web
//!   api context is gone".

